# Lichess 36-month Stage 05 + Stockfish for April 2026

This package processes **2026-04**, after its Stage-01 candidate extraction and
sequential API enrichment have completed successfully.

It performs four operations:

1. Authenticates April's Stage-01 receipt, API plan, API success receipt, every
   compact response Parquet, and every unit checkpoint.
2. Freezes the exact `status == timeout` game IDs and uses the recovered
   canonical Stage-05 producer to construct the true behavioral-opportunity
   Parquet.
3. Produces a compact, typed ZSTD Parquet input for Stockfish.
4. Runs Stockfish 18 at 100,000 nodes per position with up to ten one-thread
   worker processes in resumable 100,000-row parts.

The April target-row count is derived from the authenticated receipts and
independently checked against the Stage-01 and API Parquets. It is not assumed
in advance. The package makes no API requests.

## Isolation from the completed through-March run

The certified September/January/March Stockfish outputs are read neither as
inputs nor as mutable state. April engine outputs use the separate root:

```text
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/derived/replication_36m/stockfish100k_extension_new_api_2026_04
```

April's Stage-05 and compact-input files are added under their established
month-keyed roots without replacing earlier monthly files or checkpoints.

## Important concurrency rule

Do not run this while another Stockfish job is active on the same Mac. The
runner checks for existing `stockfish` processes and exits before production
work if it finds any. A sequential API job may continue concurrently.

## Expected runtime

Based on the completed through-March production rate:

- API/lineage authentication and Stage-05/input construction: 10–30 minutes.
- Stockfish pilot: about one minute.
- Stockfish production: approximately 6–9 hours for a typical extension month.
- Total expected wall time: approximately 6–10 hours from zero.
- The pilot prints a row-count-specific ETA before production begins.

Expected additional free space: approximately 5–10 GiB.

## Restart behavior

Rerun the same command after an interruption. Authenticated Stage-05 output,
the prepared input Parquet, and completed 100,000-row Stockfish parts are
reused. An incomplete current part may be recomputed.

## Outputs

Large ZSTD Parquet products remain on the external SSD under:

```text
/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness/derived/replication_36m/
```

The runner creates a compact result ZIP and SHA-256 sidecar in:

```text
__PRIVATE_VALUE_1__/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop
```

Upload those two files when the run completes.

